## Does the template format support shared blocks? — NO

- `src/commands/pipeline/mod.rs:309-310` — `render_prompt()` is a single `prompt.replace("{topic}", topic)`; no other placeholder/directive is processed.
- `src/commands/pipeline/definition.rs:32-55` — `load_pipeline_toml()` passes the raw file string straight to `toml::from_str`; no preprocessing pass, no include/extends/shared-block resolution.
- `src/commands/pipeline/setup.rs:66` + `setup.rs:162-164` — built-in templates are `include_str!`'d and copied verbatim (`fs::write(&file_path, template)`); no deploy-time resolution either.

**Hypothesis confirmed:** duplication is real, but extraction requires an engine preprocessing feature (template includes at load/deploy time) — a behavior-adding engine change, not a tidy. Per ticket instructions: **no code changes, no commit**; extraction left to the lead (follow-up ticket by orchestrator).

